# Viewport-Deferred Rendering and Suspense

## Context

Skaia already code-splits route pages and the 19 custom-page renderers, uses
`Suspense` around several editors, and defers large `TableView` row sets. The
loading contract is still fragmented: a 2026-08-20 inventory found 307 TSX
files, 15 files using `lazy`/`Suspense`, 9 using `IntersectionObserver`, 43 with
textual loading branches, and 23 with direct skeleton markup. The shared
`SkeletonCard` and generic route `LoadingPage` cannot accurately represent most
of those surfaces.

Custom pages expose the clearest scaling failure. `GET /pages/browse` selects
and returns every full `pages.content` document, then enriches each visible page
with per-page editor and permission calls. `CustomPages` eagerly constructs all
grid cards and parses every document as each `PageThumb` renders. Thumbnails
wait for viewport intersection, but intersection immediately mounts the complete
`BlockRenderer`; there is no hover/focus intent gate and the fallback is only
the text `Loading...`. On an actual custom page, `SectionFrame` observes the
viewport only for animation attributes: every section child mounts immediately,
starts its effects/data/media work, and uses the same generic 80px fallback.

React `Suspense` is only one part of the solution. It can show a fallback while
a lazy module resolves, but it does not by itself prevent an ordinary component
from mounting or an effect from fetching. The implementation needs explicit
viewport/intent activation, lazy module boundaries, stable content-shaped
skeleton geometry, and bounded data delivery.

## Goal

- Do not mount or start noncritical component work until its content is in or
  deliberately near the relevant viewport, with explicit eager exceptions for
  above-the-fold and interaction-critical UI.
- Make custom-page browse scale to hundreds of pages without downloading or
  parsing every page document, and load an exact renderer-based preview only
  after viewport eligibility plus hover, keyboard focus, or an accessible touch
  action.
- Defer custom-page sections independently in public view, preview, and editor
  modes while preserving the authoritative JSON document, renderer registry,
  edit/realtime behavior, and visible layout.
- Replace generic spinners/text and inaccurate rectangles with lightweight,
  themed, reduced-motion-aware skeletons that match the suspended content and
  prevent cumulative layout shift.
- Establish measurable conventions and regression gates so new heavy routes,
  panels, collections, and below-fold components adopt the same contract.

## Non-Goals

- Replacing Jotai/REST effects with a new application-wide Suspense data library
  or throwing ad-hoc promises from components.
- Deferring the header, primary navigation, focused controls, active dialogs,
  safety prompts, or the first visible route content.
- Changing `pages.content`, section schemas, preview appearance, interactive
  privacy, page-builder save/reconciliation, or WebSocket protocols.
- Unmounting an active editor, media player, form draft, or focused component
  merely because it moved offscreen.
- Treating every spinner as a defect; compact mutation/progress controls and
  decorative overlays may retain documented non-skeleton feedback.
- Replacing `MediaPlaceholder`; it remains the URL-backed media lifecycle inside
  a component once that component is activated.

## Delivery Rules

| Concern | Contract |
| --- | --- |
| Code | `React.lazy` plus a nearest useful `Suspense` boundary; imports begin only after activation when the component is noncritical. |
| Mounting | A shared viewport boundary owns intersection, root/root-margin, one-shot activation, no-observer fallback, and stable placeholder geometry. |
| Intent | Expensive previews/panels activate after deliberate hover/focus intent; touch gets an explicit accessible action. Fly-over requests are delayed/cancellable. |
| Data | Effects remain explicit and abortable unless an existing resource owns Suspense data. No fetch starts from an unactivated subtree. |
| Skeleton | Domain-shaped, token-only, `aria-busy` on the owning region, decorative bars hidden from assistive technology, reduced motion honored. |
| State | Activation must not discard focus, form/editor state, playback, realtime subscriptions, or an in-flight mutation. Activated editor sections stay mounted. |
| Failure | Chunk/data errors leave navigation and retry controls usable and are handled by a boundary scoped more narrowly than the whole app. |

## Steps

1. **Build the shared deferred-render and skeleton foundation**
   - Add a small shared viewport boundary/hook with `once`, `root`, `rootMargin`,
     disabled/eager, estimated geometry, and testable observer injection. Default
     to near-viewport preload for ordinary scrolling; use exact intersection for
     very expensive work. If `IntersectionObserver` is unavailable, render
     safely rather than leaving permanent placeholders.
   - Add an intent boundary for delayed pointer hover and keyboard focus, with
     cancellation before activation, sticky activation after a successful load,
     and an explicit touch/pen affordance. Never make preview loading a
     prerequisite for following the page link.
   - Consolidate the existing `.skeleton` styles into typed base pieces for text,
     heading, avatar, media frame, card, table row, form, chart, and content
     region. Keep domain composition beside the content it represents; do not
     create one universal fake page.
   - Add scoped async/chunk error recovery and document which null fallbacks are
     intentional decorative exceptions. Preserve existing `MediaPlaceholder`,
     `TableView` lazy rows, forum skeletons, and route lazy imports where they
     already satisfy the contract.

2. **Make custom-page browsing metadata-first and bounded**
   - Replace the `/pages/browse` response's reused full `models.Page` records
     with an explicit browse-summary DTO. Exclude `content` and other unused
     document fields, add bounded cursor pagination, and keep current search,
     visibility, ownership, editor badges, landing-page state, and action flags.
   - Replace the current per-page `GetEditors`, `IsEditor`, `CanEdit`, and admin
     checks with batched repository/service projections. Authorization and
     private/unlisted visibility remain server authoritative; do not solve the
     payload problem by exposing less-enriched but unsafe rows.
   - Add a read-only `/pages/browse/{id}/preview` contract that returns the
     caller-safe content projection only after intent. Reuse page visibility and
     interactive-response sanitization, support cancellation/ETag or revision
     validation, and keep personalized preview responses out of shared caches.
   - Update the frontend browse types independently of `PageBuilderDoc`, fetch
     additional pages at a viewport sentinel, deduplicate/abort requests, and
     keep only a bounded preview cache keyed by page ID plus revision/update time.

3. **Make preview activation intentional and exact**
   - Replace `PageThumb`'s viewport-only full render with a fixed 160px preview
     skeleton that matches the card. A card becomes eligible near the viewport
     but fetches/imports/renders only after delayed hover or focus; touch/pen
     users can explicitly load the preview without accidentally navigating.
   - Render loaded previews through the same `BlockRenderer`, section adapters,
     sanitizers, media lifecycle, and theme as page view. Use the clipped preview
     element as the section observer root so sections that cannot appear inside
     the thumbnail never mount.
   - Keep preview children inert and non-focusable, abort stale requests when a
     card is removed or its revision changes, and show distinct skeleton, empty,
     recoverable error, and ready states without layout movement.
   - Ensure list mode never requests previews and grid/card virtualization does
     not create hundreds of profiles, observers, or renderer trees at once.

4. **Defer individual custom-page sections in view and editor modes**
   - Move viewport activation into the `SectionFrame` content boundary rather
     than coupling it to the existing optional entrance animation. The frame,
     collapse control, and editor toolbar may render eagerly; the registered
     block and its effects must not mount until activated.
   - Create a `SectionSkeleton` registry keyed by canonical section type. Derive
     safe presentation hints from the existing string/object config and item
     counts so hero, cards, stats, gallery, rich text, interactive, datasource,
     code, CTA, events, profile, and unsupported sections reserve realistic
     responsive geometry without importing the real renderer.
   - Activate the first intersecting/above-fold section eagerly and near-load the
     next section for normal scroll continuity. In editor mode, pointer/focus,
     add/move/collapse actions can activate a section; once activated it remains
     mounted until page teardown so draft/editor state is never lost.
   - Preserve `mergeSections` reference stability, memoization, save debounce,
     content-free realtime refresh, interactive record privacy, page analytics,
     section animation, collapsed state, and copy/move/delete behavior. A
     skeleton must not subscribe, fetch datasource/component registries, load
     media, initialize TipTap/Monaco, or run custom code.

5. **Give routes and primary data surfaces accurate boundaries**
   - Replace the single generic full-app route fallback with route-family shells
     for custom pages, forum/thread, store/product/order/cart, documentation,
     user/profile/uploads/settings, inbox/activity, datasource/deployment/admin,
     KJV, flow, stream, and clipmaker. Keep the shared header/layout stable while
     route chunks resolve.
   - Convert current full-page textual loading states first in
     `Documentation*`, `PageManageFormPage`, `DataSourcesPage`,
     `DataSourceEditorPage`, `UserProfile`, `UserUploads`, `InboxPage`,
     `Activity`, `ThreadsFeed`, `TrashPage`, `RolesManagementPage`,
     `DeploymentsPage`, `StoreProductGrid`, and `OrderViewPage`. Reuse proven
     ProductPage/comment/forum skeleton compositions where geometry already
     matches.
   - Keep empty, loading, incremental-loading, error, and stale-refresh states
     distinct. Initial skeletons replace the target layout; pagination uses a
     small trailing/leading placeholder without hiding already loaded content.

6. **Split interaction-only and below-fold heavy modules**
   - Lazy-load analytics/Recharts only when an analytics dialog opens across
     pages and threads, with a chart-shaped modal fallback and an abortable data
     request.
   - Isolate Leaflet maps and location pickers from order/cart critical content;
     import/mount them only when their tab/panel is visible or the user elects to
     edit a location. Preserve map dimensions and delivery actions in fallback
     and error states.
   - Apply the same rule to Monaco/TipTap editors, flow/visualizer canvases,
     upload/lightbox panels, large presence/media panels, clipmaker/Twick, and
     other measured bundle/runtime hotspots. Existing eager/focused editor
     exceptions must be recorded rather than hidden behind a null fallback.
   - Use production chunk reports and runtime evidence to choose boundaries;
     avoid tiny imports that increase request overhead without reducing parse,
     execution, data, or media work.

7. **Enforce, measure, audit, and document the contract**
   - Add focused tests for observer fallback/cleanup, custom scroll roots,
     hover delay/cancellation, focus and touch activation, abort/stale response
     handling, bounded caches, section config variants, sticky editor mounts,
     error retry, and reduced motion/accessibility semantics.
   - Add backend handler/service/repository tests with private/unlisted pages and
     a hundreds-page fixture proving browse summaries omit content, pagination
     is stable, preview authorization matches page view, interactive records are
     sanitized, and query count is bounded rather than proportional to pages.
   - Add a focused loading-boundary checker or reviewed allowlist that rejects
     new route-level bare `Loading...` states, generic null fallbacks for visible
     content, and eager imports of measured heavy modules. It must allow compact
     mutation indicators and decorative overlays with reasons.
   - Capture before/after production-build chunks plus deterministic 100/500-page
     browse measurements: response bytes, SQL query count, preview requests,
     initial mounted section/card count, media/network requests before intent,
     scripting time, DOM nodes, heap, and layout shift. Set regression budgets
     from the baseline before marking the work complete.
   - Run an affected-scope auditor pass across slow/offline data, failed chunks,
     keyboard/touch, light/dark themes, reduced motion, mobile/desktop geometry,
     scroll anchoring, focus/state retention, realtime updates, and action
     availability. Update `.specs/frontend_spec`,
     `.specs/custom_page_section_compatibility_spec`,
     `.specs/custom_pages_multiplayer_spec`, `.specs/backend_spec`, and
     `.specs/caching_cdn_spec` only after the contracts are implemented.

## Verification

- Backend focused page tests cover browse DTO/pagination, batch enrichment,
  preview visibility/privacy, invalid cursors/IDs, and bounded query count.
- `env GOCACHE=/tmp/skaia-go-cache GOTMPDIR=/tmp JWT_SECRET=test-secret go test ./...`
- Frontend focused Vitest suites cover shared boundaries/skeletons,
  `CustomPages`, `SectionFrame`, `BlockRenderer`, route shells, and each migrated
  high-priority surface.
- `cd frontend && npm test -- --run`
- `cd frontend && npm run lint`
- `cd frontend && npm run build`
- `cd frontend && npm run check:media-placeholders`
- Run the new loading-boundary enforcement command.
- The 500-page fixture transfers no page `content` during browse, issues zero
  preview/media/datasource requests before intent, and does not mount offscreen
  section renderers. Hover/focus loads only the selected current revision.
- Actual page and preview use the same visible renderer output at matched widths;
  skeleton-to-content transitions retain geometry within the recorded layout-
  shift budget.
- Existing custom-page compatibility, multiplayer, interactive, media, forum,
  store, documentation, and route tests remain green.
- `git diff --check`, todo pairing/status checks, and linked-file checks pass.

